<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mita</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The mita was a system of compulsory labour in the Andes, adapted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> from an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> institution. Indigenous communities had to send a share of their men to work in mines, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of Potosi, and other enterprises. The system caused great hardship and population loss.</p></div>
